EXPERIMENT 43 – SYSTEM TESTING OF E-COMMERCE CHECKOUT PROCESS
AIM
To create test scenarios for an e-commerce checkout process for system testing. System testing checks the complete and integrated application from the user's point of view, including alternate and failure flows.
ALGORITHM
1. Study the checkout process end to end: cart, address, delivery, coupon, payment and order confirmation.
2. Identify test scenarios covering the complete, alternate and failure flows.
3. Write the steps and expected result of every scenario.
4. Execute the scenarios on the integrated system and record the status.
5. Prepare test data for users, products, coupons and successful and failed payments.
6. Verify stored data after every scenario, including order records, stock count and payment status.
7. Report failed scenarios as defects and stop.
INPUT
Pre-requisites and Test Environment
Item	Details
System under test	E-commerce website with cart, checkout and payment gateway (test mode)
Test data	Registered user, in-stock and out-of-stock products
Coupons	WELCOME10 (valid), OLD50 (expired)
Payment data	Test card for success and invalid card for failure
Technique	System testing of complete, alternate and failure flows

Test Scenarios
ID	Scenario	Test	Expected Result
CK01	Registered user checkout	Login, add product, checkout and pay by card	Order placed and confirmation displayed
CK02	Guest checkout	Add product, checkout without login and enter address	Guest order placed
CK03	Valid coupon	Enter valid coupon	Discount applied
CK04	Invalid coupon	Enter expired coupon	Error message; total unchanged
CK05	Out-of-stock product	Checkout with unavailable product	Out-of-stock message; order not placed
CK06	Payment failure	Enter invalid card number	Payment failure message; order not placed
CK07	Change delivery address	Change address before payment	New address shown in order summary
CK08	Order confirmation	Complete an order	Confirmation email/SMS sent and stock reduced
CK09	Cancel an order	Cancel before shipment	Order cancelled and amount refunded
CK10	Session timeout	Keep payment page idle for 15 minutes	Session expires and cart is retained

OUTPUT
Test Execution Summary
Total Designed	Executed	Passed	Failed	Blocked	Pass %
10	10	10	0	0	100%

All 10 test scenarios passed.
RESULT
Thus, the test scenarios of the e-commerce checkout process were created and executed for system testing. Normal, alternate and failure flows were tested, and the output was verified.
